    "explanation": "Rider — you get the SGD 4.50 back. Driver — the fee does not stand, but not because anyone acted in bad faith.\n\nThe timeline is common ground. The trip record shows you arrived at Northpoint City at 13:31:56 and terminated the trip at 13:34:24 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace puts you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE pickup geofence from 13:31:56 — the first qualifying in-geofence fix matches your arrival marker exactly, with speed 0.0 km/h — and you held position until 13:34:20. That is 144 seconds of continuous in-geofence dwell; the derived arrival block reports the same figures (longest_run_sec 144.0; run_count 1; shortfall_sec 36.0).\n\nThe free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; fee_schedule.defaults agrees). POL-NS-01 limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least 180 seconds, measured from the first qualifying fix. 144 seconds is 36 seconds short, so limb (c) fails and the baseline charge cannot stand. Limb (d) is also short on timing: the cancellation at 13:34:24 came about 32 seconds before the 180-second dwell would have run out at 13:34:56. POL-NS-06 then applies directly: where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the free waiting period, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded. The amount refunded is the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line (fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee 4.50; total_charged 4.50; payment_status CHARGED; refund_issued_sgd 0.00). No booking or platform fee was charged on this cancelled trip.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-06 withholds it on a shortfall, and POL-NS-07's payout engages only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full — which it is not.\n\nOn the claims. For the driver: the points that POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied (arrived event present; first qualifying in-geofence fix coinciding with it) and that limb (d)'s reason code is RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three recognised codes, are accepted as facts — but the fee still fails on limb (c), and the cancellation preceded the dwell completing. The POL-NS-04 point is accepted: the driver did reply 'ok' at 13:33:11, 15 seconds after the rider's 13:32:56 message, so the rider-contact clause does not exonerate the rider; that simply leaves the case where POL-NS-06 already puts it. The description of the present state (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is accurate, but NO_ACTION is rejected as the outcome: POL-NS-06 licenses FULL_REFUND. The claim for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.60 (80 percent of 4.50) is rejected, because POL-NS-07 pays only on a fee that stands. The points that the arrival marker is not false (inside the radius, stationary at the arrival timestamp, so POL-NS-05 is not engaged) and that POL-NS-03 does not govern are accepted, and no false-arrival referral arises.\n\nFor the rider: the POL-NS-06 arithmetic is accepted and decides the case. The POL-NS-04 point is accepted as to the message being a locating statement ('im at the lobby, coming out'), and the rider track does place the device within about 18.4 m of the pin across all 45 fixes — but POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate because the driver replied within 120 seconds, so the refund comes from POL-NS-06, not that clause. The SGD 4.50 figure is accepted. The argument that limb (d) fails because the driver's statement ('I had another booking waiting') shows a motive other than the rider's failure to appear is rejected: POL-NS-01(d) reads the trip_record's cancellation_reason_code, which is RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three recognised codes, and the driver's separate statement is not one of that limb's tests; in any event the fee already fails on limb (c), so nothing turns on it.\n\nImpairment and weight. Nothing the ruling rests on is impaired: the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown all carry weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue