    "explanation": "Rider, the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02707 is refunded to you in full. Driver, the fee was not chargeable on this trip and no compensation is payable.\n\nThe arithmetic is not in dispute and the record is clean. The trip was accepted at 13:26:38, the 'arrived' event is at 13:31:56, and the cancellation is at 13:34:24 (EV-TRIP-02707). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02707) shows one continuous qualifying stay inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, from 13:31:56 to 13:34:20 — 144 seconds — with 100% coverage, 10-second cadence, 52 fixes and no gaps. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (EV-TRIP-02707), which is what POL-NS-01(c) directs. The effective in-geofence dwell therefore falls 36 seconds short of the required minimum. Under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and the cancellation-fee line is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. The amount refunded is the SGD 4.50 shown on EV-FARE-02707 (total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). No base, distance, time or platform fee was charged on this cancelled trip, so the whole contested SGD 4.50 is returned.\n\nDriver, your points are answered. You are right that POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) hold: the trip record carries an 'arrived' event, and the trace places you inside the geofence from 13:31:56, with the arrival marker matching the first qualifying in-geofence fix exactly and your speed there at 0.0 kph, so POL-NS-05 does not make the marker false and the waiting clock was not started early. You are also right that cancellation_reason_code is RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) reads, and that this is not a wrong-entrance case under POL-NS-03, your stationary fixes being inside the 120 m radius rather than outside it. But limb (c) fails: 144 seconds is short of the 180-second free waiting